h", "a", "stipulation", "that", "they", "never", "resume", "their", "animal", "breeding", "activities", ".", "The", "implications", "are", "clear", ":", "a", "drop", "in", "global", "food", "availability", "and", "an", "inevitable", "spike", "in", "prices", ".", "Remember", "Sri", "Lanka", "\u2019s", "ill", "-", "fated", "venture", "into", "100", "%", "organic", "farming", "?", "The", "island", "nation", "faced", "a", "humanitarian", "nightmare", "with", "a", "staggering", "90", "%", "of", "its", "population", "on", "the", "brink", "of", "starvation", ".", "Read", "more", ":", "Globalists", "\u2019", "war", "on", "the", "world", "\u2019s", "food", "supply"], "sentence": "Globalists\u2019 war on the world\u2019s food supply \n\n So, what\u2019s this newfound hostility against the thing that keeps us alive? Take a deep breath. Farming uses nitrogen, and suddenly, nitrogen is the new antagonist in the tale of global warming. The narrative is simple: eliminate nitrogen, and save the world. Yet, in the name of \u201cpreservation,\u201d entire segments of our food production are under siege. Consider rice \u2013 a staple for half the world\u2019s population. Renowned agencies claim, \u201cRice accounts for roughly 10% of global methane emissions,\u201d emphasising the urgent need to curtail its production. But the ramifications? Starvation for billions. Look to the Netherlands for further evidence. Dutch farmers, the backbone of a nation that is a leading exporter of meat and agricultural products, are being chased off their lands. A staggering number, 3,000 farms, are forecasted to be confiscated in the coming years. The tragic fallout is evident, with a reported 20 to 30 farmers tragically ending their lives annually. Our friends in Europe are no strangers to these baffling decisions either. The European Commission greenlit a strategy to compensate livestock farmers for halting their operations in certain areas \u2013 with a stipulation that they never resume their animal breeding activities. The implications are clear: a drop in global food availability and an inevitable spike in prices. Remember Sri Lanka\u2019s ill-fated venture into 100% organic farming? The island nation faced a humanitarian nightmare with a staggering 90% of its population on the brink of starvation. Read more: Globalists\u2019 war on the world\u2019s food supply", "language": "en", "metadata": {"sentence_id": "1"}, "frames": [{"name": "Store", "roles": [{"name": "Resource", "filler": "food", "idxs": [7, 7]}, {"name": "Supply", "filler": "supply", "idxs": [8, 8]}], "idxs": [8, 8], "activation": "supply"}, {"name": "Dead_or_alive", "roles": [{"name": "Protagonist", "filler": "us", "idxs": [21, 21]}], "idxs": [22, 22], "activation": "alive"}, {"name": "Cause_to_continue", "roles": [{"name": "Cause", "filler": "that", "idxs": [19, 19]}, {"name": "State", "filler": "alive", "idxs": [22, 22]}, {"name": "Process", "filler": "us", "idxs": [21, 21]}, {"name": "Cause", "filler": "the thing", "idxs": [17, 18]}], "idxs": [20, 20], "activation": "keeps"}, {"name": "Hostile_encounter", "roles": [{"name": "Side_2", "filler": "against the thing that keeps us alive", "idxs": [16, 22]}], "idxs": [15, 15], "activation": "hostility"}, {"name": "Food", "roles": [{"name": "Food", "filler": "food", "idxs": [7, 7]}], "idxs": [7, 7], "activation": "food"}, {"name": "Hostile_encounter", "roles": [{"name": "Side_1", "filler": "Globalists \u2019", "idxs": [0, 1]}, {"name": "Issue", "filler": "on the world \u2019s food supply", "idxs": [3, 8]}], "idxs": [2, 2], "activation": "war"}, {"name": "Political_locales", "roles": [{"name": "Locale", "filler": "world", "idxs": [5, 5]}], "idxs": [5, 5], "activation": "world"}, {"name": "Importance", "roles": [{"name": "Factor", "filler": "breath", "idxs": [27, 27]}], "idxs": [26, 26], "activation": "deep"}, {"name": "Breathing", "roles": [{"name": "Manner", "filler": "deep", "idxs": [26, 26]}, {"name": "Air", "filler": "breath", "idxs": [27, 27]}